{"batch":"mathematics-grade11-analytical-geometry","source":"DBE CAPS Mathematics FET Grades 10–12","units":[{"unitId":"mathematics-g11-analytical-geometry","title":"Straight-line geometry","why":"Coordinate geometry turns geometric relationships into equations that can be tested and used in design.","objectives":["calculate gradient and distance","find midpoint","derive a line equation"],"definitions":["gradient","intercept","midpoint","parallel","perpendicular"],"principles":["m=(y2-y1)/(x2-x1)","distance=√((Δx)²+(Δy)²)","perpendicular gradients multiply to -1"],"examples":["Gradient through (1,2),(5,10) is 2","Midpoint of (2,4),(8,10) is (5,7)"],"misconceptions":["reversing only one coordinate difference","assuming parallel lines have equal intercepts"],"practice":["Find gradient through (0,1),(4,9).","Find midpoint (2,6),(8,10).","Find distance between (0,0),(3,4).","Write line with gradient 2 through (1,3).","Find gradient perpendicular to 4.","Test whether (1,2),(3,6) lie on y=2x.","Explain how to identify parallel lines.","Find x-intercept y=3x-6."],"solutions":["2","(5,8)","5","y=2x+1","-1/4","yes","equal gradients","x=2"],"quizQuestions":["State gradient formula.","Midpoint of (0,0),(4,6)?","Distance formula?","Gradient of a horizontal line?","Perpendicular to 2?","What is an intercept?","Equation y=mx+c meaning?","How test collinearity?","Parallel gradient rule?","Name one coordinate-geometry use."],"diagram":"content/diagrams/coordinate-line.svg","videoPackage":{"title":"Lines on a coordinate plane","duration":"9 minutes","scenes":["plot points","gradient triangle","distance","midpoint","line equation"],"transcript":"We plot two points, measure vertical and horizontal change, and use the gradient and midpoint rules to describe the line precisely."}}]}
